              <div class="case-topline"><span>Personal ops</span><h3>Contact saving and cleanup</h3><p>When Henry says “save this contact,” Ada treats Apple/iCloud Contacts as the source of truth and avoids inventing a second address book.</p></div>
              <dl>
                <div><dt>When it runs</dt><dd>On demand when Henry sends a person, number, email, or follow-up instruction.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>What it connects to</dt><dd>Apple/iCloud Contacts, provided details, conversation context, duplicate checks, and relationship notes when allowed.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>What Henry gets back</dt><dd>A saved or updated contact, duplicate warning, and the exact fields changed.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Where the human stays in charge</dt><dd>Creating or updating the intended local contact is safe when requested. Messaging the person, enriching externally, or changing unrelated records needs approval.</dd></div>
              </dl>
            </article>
            <article class="case-card featured-card">
              <div class="uc-figure"><img src="/use-cases/plan-grill.webp" alt="Illustration: Plan grill" width="1024" height="576" loading="lazy" /></div>
